%S A397968 1,2,15,250,8773,619404,86881207,24207005464,13434318694304,
%T A397968 14881970817508752,32942680867632431864,145791545619077922202094,
%U A397968 1290253109698044379252890547,22836267726487388136626373828606,808347354429793670920820958305586616
%N A397968 Number of reducible flow graphs on n unlabeled nodes: digraphs with a distinguished entry from which every node is reachable and in which every cycle has a unique entry node, counted up to isomorphism fixing the entry.
%C A397968 Reducible control-flow graphs up to entry-preserving isomorphism, self-loops disallowed.
%C A397968 Also the number of reducible single-source digraphs with self-loops allowed: the loop-encoding bijection of A351052 (replace each edge x -> entry by a self-loop at x) preserves reducibility, since edges into the entry are always back edges.
%C A397968 Computed exactly by Burnside summation over the cycle types of the entry-fixing permutations: the number of reducible flow graphs invariant under a given permutation satisfies an equivariant version of the labeled SCC-decomposition recurrence, with blocks generalized to block orbits (an orbit's return map is a header-fixing automorphism of its block) and edge counts to invariant-edge-orbit counts; see _reducible_unlabeled in the linked program.
%D A397968 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A397968 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A397968 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A397968 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A397968 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%H A397968 Gregory Morse, <a href="/A397968/a397968.py.txt">Python program</a>, Aug 2026.
%e A397968 a(n) = (1/(n-1)!) * Sum over cycle types mu of n-1 elements of permcount(mu) * F_R(mu), where F_R is the equivariant SCC-region recurrence: SCC blocks are replaced by block orbits, their return maps fix the region headers, and available cross edges are replaced by invariant edge orbits.
%o A397968 (Python) unlabeled_reducible_sequence("unlabeled_reducible_cfgs", 16) # See link for program code.
%Y A397968 Cf. A351052 (all such digraphs).
%K A397968 nonn,new
%O A397968 1,2
%A A397968 _Gregory Morse_, Aug 13 2026
